{"title":"Convolution","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>convolution</b> of two functions can mean various things.\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\"> number theoretic</a> context, convolution of two functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/0/d10b74eb3bc0e338abb29ec5dacfe20847d4c89b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f,g : \\mathbb{N} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> usually means <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dirichlet_convolution\" title=\"Dirichlet convolution\">Dirichlet convolution</a>, defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/5/8651768f3d699b39ab86628c93aced37e78b9957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f * g = \\sum_{d\\mid n} f(d)g\\left( \\frac{n}{d} \\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"175\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Analysis\" title=\"Analysis\"> analytic</a> context, convolution of functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/0/1d0478c3240a609d4968f6a3b9ea994476d87424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle f, g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> usually means a function of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c86a79eac11bb6c619e0c35a2d88a1079879a2e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int f(\\tau) g(t-\\tau) d\\tau$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"137\" height=\"39\" />. \n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Convolution&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183436\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.010 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 837/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.320      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.320      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4994:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183436 and revision id 15175. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}